      "content": "Which ONE of the following statements is CORRECT for an ELECTROLYTIC CELL?\nA. The anode is the positive electrode.\nB. The cathode is the positive electrode.\nC. Oxidation takes place at the cathode.\nD. Reduction takes place at the anode.\n\nI’m confident it’s B, because I thought the cathode is always positive."
